# AuditGate has no local secrets today.
#
# The Jira app reads and writes only Forge storage and Jira, so it needs no keys.
# The Bitbucket app (Phase 2) will store a Jira API token through its own settings page,
# in Forge secret storage, never in a file.
#
# If a value is ever needed at runtime, set it with:
#   forge variables set --encrypt NAME value
# and document the NAME here, never the value.
